    "['set firewall family inet filter [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.1.10/24\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n ip address 10.1.1.10 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Huawei, interfaces are configured directly without \"unit\" designation\\n2. The subnet mask is specified in dotted decimal format (255.255.255.0) instead of prefix length (/24)\\n3. The interface naming convention is similar but with capital letters in Huawei (GigabitEthernet vs ge)', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip address 10.1.1.10 255.255.255.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip address 10.1.1.10 255.255.255.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.1.10/24\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n ip address 10.1.1.10 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Huawei, interfaces are configured directly without \"unit\" designation\\n2. The subnet mask is specified in dotted decimal format (255.255.255.0) instead of prefix length (/24)\\n3. The interface naming convention is similar but with capital letters in Huawei (GigabitEthernet vs ge)', 'trans_template': 'ip address 10.1.1.10 255.255.255.0'}]]": 1,
