    "['unit [parameter2] tunnel key [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface Tunnel0/0/0', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ninterface Tunnel0/0/0\\ntunnel-key 0\\n##\\n\\nThe Juniper command `set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel key 0` configures a GRE tunnel key (0 in this case) for interface gr-0/0/0. The equivalent HUAWEI command sets the same tunnel key parameter under the tunnel interface configuration mode. \\n\\nNote: \\n1. HUAWEI uses interface naming like \"Tunnel0/0/0\" instead of Juniper\\'s \"gr-0/0/0\"\\n2. The parameter name is `tunnel-key` (with hyphen) in HUAWEI instead of `tunnel key` (with space) in Juniper', 'trans_template': 'interface Tunnel0/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tunnel-key 0', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ninterface Tunnel0/0/0\\ntunnel-key 0\\n##\\n\\nThe Juniper command `set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel key 0` configures a GRE tunnel key (0 in this case) for interface gr-0/0/0. The equivalent HUAWEI command sets the same tunnel key parameter under the tunnel interface configuration mode. \\n\\nNote: \\n1. HUAWEI uses interface naming like \"Tunnel0/0/0\" instead of Juniper\\'s \"gr-0/0/0\"\\n2. The parameter name is `tunnel-key` (with hyphen) in HUAWEI instead of `tunnel key` (with space) in Juniper', 'trans_template': 'tunnel-key 0'}]]": 1,
    "['set security ipsec vpn <profile-name> bind-interface [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipsec profile <profile-name> binding tunnel interface Tunnel0/0/0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ipsec profile <profile-name> binding tunnel interface Tunnel0/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Huawei equivalent command for the Juniper IPsec VPN binding configuration:\\n\\n##\\nipsec profile <profile-name> binding tunnel interface Tunnel0/0/0\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Huawei, \"Tunnel0/0/0\" is commonly used as the equivalent GRE tunnel interface name (instead of Juniper\\'s gr-0/0/0)\\n2. The IPsec profile binding command in Huawei directly associates the profile with the tunnel interface\\n3. The angle brackets <profile-name> should be replaced with your actual profile name, same as in the original Juniper configuration', 'trans_template': 'ipsec profile <profile-name> binding tunnel interface Tunnel0/0/0'}]]": 1,
