    "['set routing-options static route [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip route-static 172.16.1.0 255.255.255.0 NULL0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip route-static 172.16.1.0 255.255.255.0 NULL0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nip route-static 172.16.1.0 255.255.255.0 NULL0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper \"static route ... discard\" command creates a blackhole route that drops traffic to the specified prefix.\\n- In Huawei, the equivalent is \"ip route-static\" with NULL0 as the next-hop interface (similar to Juniper\\'s discard).\\n- The subnet mask is specified in dotted decimal format (255.255.255.0) instead of prefix length notation (/24).\\n- NULL0 is Huawei\\'s equivalent of Juniper\\'s discard interface.', 'trans_template': 'ip route-static 172.16.1.0 255.255.255.0 NULL0'}]]": 1,
    "['set routing-options static route [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip route-static 10.1.1.0 255.255.255.0 NULL0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip route-static 10.1.1.0 255.255.255.0 NULL0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nip route-static 10.1.1.0 255.255.255.0 NULL0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei devices, the `discard` action in Juniper is equivalent to `NULL0` interface in Huawei, which silently drops packets. The subnet mask is specified in dotted decimal format (255.255.255.0) instead of CIDR notation (/24).', 'trans_template': 'ip route-static 10.1.1.0 255.255.255.0 NULL0'}]]": 1,
